	(footprint "USB4105-GF-A"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "6844c9fe-abc6-4027-a494-6385ee50a217")
		(at 100.73 87.53 -90)
		(descr "GCT USB4105-GF-A USB Type-C receptacle, top mount, 16 contacts on 12 pads, 8.94 x 7.35 x 3.31 mm. Land pattern: case_usb4105.pdf p.1 'Recommended PCB Layout' (rev B4, component side view): 12 pads 1.15 mm long at y = -3.68 mm; wide pads 0.6 mm (A1/B12 x -3.2, A4/B9 x -2.4, B4/A9 x +2.4, A12/B1 x +3.2), narrow pads 0.3 mm (B8 -1.75, A5 -1.25, B7 -0.75, A6 -0.25, A7 +0.25, B6 +0.75, A8 +1.25, B5 +1.75); two holes dia 0.65 mm at x +-2.89 y -2.605; four shell slots at x +-4.32: y -3.105 (pad 1.0 x 2.1 mm, drill 0.6 x 1.7) and y +1.075 (pad 1.0 x 1.8 mm, drill 0.6 x 1.4). Pin table (p.1): A1, A12, B1, B12 GND, A4, A9, B4, B9 VBUS, A5 CC1, B5 CC2, A6 Dp1, A7 Dn1, B6 Dp2, B7 Dn2, A8 SBU1, B8 SBU2, SHELL (no number: the four shell pads are all numbered SH). Two contacts share each wide pad, so both pad numbers sit on the same copper. Mating face at y = +4.18 mm (courtyard line of the drawing).")
